<article class="env-example" id="B7E654">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/B7E654">Example <span data-tag="B7E654">8.2.1.2</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be any category which admits small limits and colimits. Then $\calC $ can be endowed with the <em>trivial</em> model structure: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(W)$"><p>
The weak equivalences in $\calC $ are the isomorphisms. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(C)$"><p>
Every morphism in $\calC $ is a cofibration. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(F)$"><p>
Every morphism in $\calC $ is a fibration. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>